Subject: [PROPOSED, NOT APPLIED] FUSION-SKETCH-TOOLS-BEHAVIOR-003 product contract
Base: c1959b1e84a7c38288022622a9585a38c07d3f7e

Status: PROPOSED_NOT_IMPLEMENTED / BLOCKED_PRODUCT_CODE_START.
This patch is a review artifact. It has not been applied to src/, vendor/,
tests/, spec/, release/, or package.json. Product audit authorization is required.

Scope:
- Existing sketch.line/sketch.arc receive typed creationIntent; geometry,
  inferred constraints and dimensions execute under the existing one-command
  CadApplicationImpl before-snapshot. No nested execute or second history.
- Origin, midpoint and direction use coordinate_x/y, p2p_symmetric_ppp and
  p2p_angle in the same existing PlaneGCS instance. No auxiliary axis geometry.
- Angular angleSense stores the selected forward/interior measure and turn
  branch with ordered semantic Line refs. Interior 120 remains 120 for Save/Open
  and setValue; only runtime maps it to solver 60 and swaps refs for clockwise.
  Missing angleSense preserves legacy schema-v3 ordered-forward behavior.
- Line/Arc Coincident and Tangent use the existing native adapter support.
  Clockwise input explicitly maps input start to canonical Arc.b.
- Persisted grammar becomes schema 4, with explicit v3 migration and a fixture.
  Legacy grammars remain frozen; load does not write storage.
- Focused executable tests cover atomic undo/redo, rejected substep rollback,
  solved 40 mm at 30 deg, origin, dependent midpoint, closed chain,
  clockwise/counterclockwise tangent Arc and serialization. The separate angular
  sense regression defines 16 real-solver cases (2 bearings, 2 values, 2 senses,
  2 branches), atomic creation, native-value edits, Save/Open, invalid selectors,
  rejected mixed orientation and frozen-schema migration guards.

Limits:
- This is atomic command/history composition, not an async solve transaction.
  CadApplicationImpl.execute still publishes before later recompute. A failed
  later solve is not silently rolled back by this patch.
- Native gesture timing, UI inference arbitration, numeric focus/Tab/Escape,
  annotation placement and conflict recovery require the authorized UI slice.
- Angular/direction editing still needs the shared parameter panel to carry
  the selected dimension unit/type and expose the semantic selector. Existing
  common setValue preserves angleSense and edits the selected stored value;
  its current UI edit panel still has the old mm default. Document-tree labels
  use the stored value and degree unit; no complementary-value relabel is used.
- Angular values 0 and 180 remain excluded by the existing strict angular range.
  No degenerate-angle solve behavior or complete native angle UI is claimed.
- Full geometry/OCC, UI, migration-host and exact-HEAD CI gates must be run in a
  separately authorized product worktree before acceptance. They were not run
  to produce this artifact. No product acceptance or delivery is claimed.
- The future diff exceeds the 20-handwritten-file architecture review trigger,
  mostly because adding persisted grammar requires host/schema test updates.
  It does not grow frozen useSketchDimensionController; other frozen owners
  and CadApplicationImpl are unchanged.

Mapping evidence (existing baseline only, not execution of this proposal):
  D2-R2 external regression-precommit/angle-contract-probe-20261107.json
  within ASA-CAD-Fusion-Captures/sketch-tools-behavior-003-20261107.
  Probe SHA-256: 4d9ead77a474d034f26abc9be9a7ad32613af0f07e8dc9f7635e71cd1177540f.
  The observed positive PlaneGCS angle uses ordered forward refs; reversed refs
  select the opposite branch. Solver convergence alone does not establish the
  requested branch. The new regression therefore asserts actual endpoints.

